{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794565886,"nonce":"h+DlW/6EFalaE0xcKYoJrAJ4lIg=","message":"The generator now accepts i64 parameters and results in lent Haxe functions. Haxe sees haxe.Int64; the adapter carries each callback i64 as the existing eight-byte data encoding. Ordinary methods and asynchronous i64 results keep their existing representation. No ABI, future, or runtime support code changed, and no unsafe code was added.\n\nA direct native callback representation was tested first and rejected: Ash JIT returned the floating-point bit pattern 0x43b2345678765432 for the integer 0x1234567876543210. Reusing the data callback path avoids dynamic numeric conversions on every runtime and reuses the existing bytes trampolines instead of adding runtime-specific boxing.\n\nThe counter fixture covers both directions, callbacks with no parameters, mixed text and i64 arguments, signed limits, values above floating-point precision, bitwise operations, exception identity, and a successful call after a failure. Generator checks cover a callback mixing bool, i64, f64, and i32. The fixture manifest and both design/convention documents were updated.\n\nValidation on macOS arm64 with Ash 0.1.17:\n- cargo test --workspace, cargo fmt --all -- --check, and cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings pass.\n- All nine counter modes pass: hl and gen-hl on Ash, cpp, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, wasm, gen-wasm, emcc, gen-emcc. Native Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter and hxcpp/CPPIA programs were repeated three times each. Wasm and Emscripten programs were repeated twice after their initial passes.\n- CLI and examples pass on Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm, and Emscripten. C imports (including sqlite3 where supported) pass on Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, and Emscripten.\n\nThe test runners use timeouts. Fresh temporary crates needed CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true to use cached dependencies within the network sandbox; Emscripten needed a copy of its SDK cache in /private/tmp because the installed cache is outside the writable sandbox.\n\nNot run: stock HashLink (no executable installed), Linux, Windows, or a second machine. Mobile tests were not run because compilation/linking behavior did not change; Miri was not run because hxn-abi and hxn-future did not change.\n\nThe change is uncommitted. The broader generator issue stays open for its remaining gaps.","files":null}]}